# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quartus build products (from Template_MiSTer, kept in step with it)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
db
greybox_tmp
incremental_db
output_files
simulation
hc_output
scaler
hps_isw_handoff
vip
*_sim
.qsys_edit
PLLJ_PLLSPE_INFO.txt
*.qdf
*.rpt
*.smsg
*.summary
*.done
*.jdi
*.pin
*.sof
*.qws
*.ppf
*.ddb
*.sopcinfo
*.csv
*.f
# ...but NOT a testbench file list. `*.f` above is Quartus scratch; sim/<tb>/files.f
# is the source of truth for what scripts/run_jt_unit.sh compiles, and it was
# silently unstaged until this exception existed.
!sim/**/files.f
*.cmp
*.sip
*.spd
*.bsf
*.xml
*_netlist
*.cdf
build_id.v
c5_pin_model_dump.txt

# Staged-build worktree (scripts/build_staged.py): each build compiles a
# snapshot of HEAD there, so Quartus scratch stays out of the repo root and
# the main tree stays editable during the compile. See docs/WORKFLOW.md.
build/
quartus_*.log
q_*.log
sta*.log
worst_*.rpt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ModelSim / Verilator
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
work/
transcript
vsim.wlf
modelsim.ini
*.vstf
sim/**/*.log
sim/**/*.bin
sim/**/*.lst
sim/**/*.hex
sim/**/*.raw
sim/**/*.trace
sim/**/*.dec
sim/**/*dump*.txt
sim/**/fixture.txt
# Vendored cores' SIMULATION-only dumps, written into whatever CWD the
# simulator runs from.
/*.raw
obj_verilator/
simout/
# Icarus waveform dumps from jotego's unit benches (scripts/run_jt_unit.sh)
sim/**/*.lxt
sim/**/*.vcd

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copyrighted MAME ROM dumps -- used locally for bring-up and for building the
# ROM images the .mra files describe. NEVER committed, in any subdirectory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
roms/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local hardware-debug scratch: screenshots pulled back off the MiSTer,
# decoded probe captures, ad-hoc analysis output. Regenerable, and only
# meaningful alongside the temporary debug build that produced them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root-only: this is the MAME capture directory. Anchored with a leading slash
# because a bare `debug/` matches ANY directory of that name at any depth,
# which on the Fuuki core silently swallowed rtl/debug/ -- the core's own
# instrumentation source.
/debug/
/*.png
/*.txt
scratch_*.png
scratch_*.txt
cfg.bin
outfile.bin

# MAME's own state directories, written into whatever directory MAME was
# launched from. scripts/mame_capture.py runs it from MAME_DIR, but a hand-run
# probe from the repository root leaves these behind.
cfg/
nvram/
snap/
sta/

# Local MiSTer connection settings (host/user/password) for the deploy
# scripts -- never committed.
mister.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# releases/ IS the right home for built bitstreams, but only a build VERIFIED
# to actually run the games belongs in git. Committing one that merely
# compiles is actively misleading. Add a good one deliberately:
#   git add -f "releases/<name>.rbf"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
releases/*.rbf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standalone synth-check scratch (rtl/synth_check/): a Quartus project of its
# own, so its logs and reports are build products like any other.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
compile.log
worst.tcl

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build products of the vendored jtframe tool (tools/jtframe/build.sh). The Go
# SOURCE is committed; the binary and Go's module cache are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/jtframe/jtframe.exe
build/jtbin/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS / Python scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*~
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
